# Integer16 widening assignment rejected

Verifies arithmetic promotion remains local to registered operators and does
not introduce implicit widening when assigning an int8 value directly to an
int16 variable.

>>> source
narrow: int8 = 127
wide: int16 = narrow
print(wide)

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: type mismatch: variable `wide` expects `int16`, expression produces `int8` at Span { start: 33, end: 39 }

<<< exit
1
